{
  "title": "DocumentCodec",
  "description": "AssetSourceCodec for an asset whose source file is a persisted, versioned document (`{ \"$type\": ..., \"$version\": ..., ...body }`). The representation kept in a cache is the text exactly as it arrived, frame and original version included. Migrations and validation run on every decode, after the cache and before the factory, so shipping a newer document version with new migrations reads records cached by an older release without a cache miss and without a layout version bump. Any failure to read the document - malformed JSON, a foreign `$type`, a newer or discontinued `$version`, a failing migration, a body the parser rejects - is an AssetDecodeError naming the type, with the specific error as its `cause`. A factory only ever sees a validated current-version body.",
